# Cron jobs (local-cron-jobs) every machine installs.
#
# This file is read live, not only as a sample (sd:8607): the cron stage
# reads it beside the machine's own roster, so a job named here installs on
# every machine through the refresh, with no line added by hand to each
# machine's <config>/machine-setup/profiles/common.cron. A machine refuses
# one with a `!<job>` line in its own <profile>.cron. Every other file in
# this folder is a sample to copy.
#
# A job named here needs its job file in <config>/cron-jobs/jobs/ or an
# example in local-cron-jobs/examples/, which the stage installs for it.
#
# fseventsd-hourly repairs a runaway fseventsd (local-fseventsd, sd:8579);
# every machine runs the same daemon, so every machine runs the job. It needs
# <config>/fseventsd/.env for anything to happen; without it the run exits 3,
# nothing to check, which the job passes as 0. The envs stage installs that
# .env from local-fseventsd/.env.example.
fseventsd-hourly
